  {
    "first_name": "Nicol\u00e1s",
    "last_name": "Torres-Echeverry",
    "full_name": "Nicol\u00e1s Torres-Echeverry",
    "email": "nte@uchicago.edu",
    "institution": "University of Chicago",
    "bio": "Nicolas Torres-Echeverry is a Ph.D. candidate in the Sociology Department at the University of Chicago, a Neubauer Distinguished Doctoral Fellow, and a 2024-2025 Jennings Randolph Peace Scholar Fellow at USIP. His research and teaching interests intersect political sociology, war and peace, political organization, internet and society, sociology of culture, and urban sociology, with a regional focus on Latin America. His multi-method research examines the link between civil society and political organization in the Global South and their interaction with cultural representations in contemporary political transformations. He is particularly interested in bridging qualitative and computational methods through abductive research.",
    "personal_website": "https://voices.uchicago.edu/nte/",
